### 1. Free License: Learning & Academic Research
(a) Any individual or non-profit organization may freely use, copy, modify,
compile and display this software and its source code for **non-commercial
purposes** — including learning, teaching, academic research and paper
reproducibility — without a separate written license.
(b) Any such use must retain this copyright notice and license text, and must
cite the authors and the public repository (and the arXiv version when the
paper is published) in publications and public demos.
(c) THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. The
authors are not liable for any direct or indirect damage arising from its use.

### 2. Commercial License
(a) Any **commercial use** of this software or of modified/derivative/integrated
works based on it — including, but not limited to, embedding in commercial
products, offering paid services / SaaS, reselling, closed-source
redistribution, or profit-oriented deployment and further development — requires
a **prior written commercial license** signed with the copyright holder.
(b) Unauthorized commercial use is an infringement; the authors reserve all
rights to enforce these terms.

### 3. General
(a) This license does not transfer any trademark or patent rights.
Contributions are accepted on the understanding that they are released under
this same dual license.
(b) Third-party components shipped with the project (e.g. `src/model/stb_image.h`;
llama.cpp-derived kernels in `tools/llama_gemm_q4_0_4x4_asm.c` and the
ggml_gemm/gemv/vec_dot ports marked in `src/model/vllm_safetensors.c`)
remain under their own respective licenses — stb_image.h: MIT, Copyright (c)
2017 Sean Barrett; llama.cpp code: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
authors (full notices at the top of the respective files). The dual-license
terms above apply only to the project's original code, not to those portions.
(c) Model weights, datasets and conversion artifacts are NOT distributed in
this repository; follow the original sources' licenses if you use them.

